From 7843373b035571ab500e8df0431cdcea3a5c618f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abdulaziz Al-Tamimi <attmimi.abdul@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:02:37 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] F-D: Tadawul disclosures from Argaam's market-wide lists

Argaam stopped filling each company's Disclosures list (section 204) in 2026-03;
its market-wide lists (244 English, 245 Arabic, market 3) still update. New
argaam/tools/market_disclosures.py reads them each night, gives each article to the
ticker its page names (DMP_CompanySymbol), and keeps a manifest per ticker that
evidence_builder.py reads as disclosures (same item ids as before, so no repeats).
nightly_pipeline.sh runs it after the scrape, before the rebuild; its line goes into
the OK status. Never fatal.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
